Z||000000||N_Man||07-13-2000||01:34 AM||||I know that many of you have had high speed sway.  I did to untill today.<BR>I bought the car with so many problems that the sway was way down on the list to fix and now im running out of problems to fix  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>When I did the engine I put the cradle back in with poly bushings, sway was now scary at 110kph instead of 90kph.  But today I replaced my swaybar endlinks with heaavyduty units and poly bushings (one was snapped when i got the car), sway is GONE took the car up to 140kph for the fist time and it was very stable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Just thought Id let the sufferers of sway know to check the condidion of their endlinks.  I hope this helps||||reg||6
Z||000001||AL||07-13-2000||08:15 PM||||put a sway bar in the rear and it will stay put alot more, that's what i did.||||reg||14
